# 03 — Security: Mandatory Rules

## 🔒 The Non-Negotiables
1. **Supabase RLS is MANDATORY on every table** — no exceptions
2. **Service role key NEVER goes to client** — not even accidentally
3. **`.env` is NEVER committed** — use `.gitignore` and Cloudflare env vars
4. **Google OAuth is handled by Supabase Auth** — no custom JWT implementation
5. **All user data access goes through RLS** — no bypassing with service role on client

---

## Supabase RLS Pattern (Every Table)

Every table MUST have RLS enabled and a policy. Never create a table without policies.

```sql
-- Enable RLS on every table (MANDATORY)
ALTER TABLE notes ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Users can only see their own data
CREATE POLICY "Users can read own notes"
ON notes FOR SELECT
USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

CREATE POLICY "Users can insert own notes"
ON notes FOR INSERT
WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

CREATE POLICY "Users can update own notes"
ON notes FOR UPDATE
USING (auth.uid() = user_id)
WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

CREATE POLICY "Users can delete own notes"
ON notes FOR DELETE
USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- Public data (e.g., blog posts, public scores)
CREATE POLICY "Public can read published posts"
ON posts FOR SELECT
USING (is_published = true);
```

> **Rule**: If a table has no policy, Supabase blocks ALL access by default (with RLS on).
> Never disable RLS on a table. Never use `FOR ALL USING (true)` on user data tables.

