## Secrets Management

### ✅ Safe
```bash
# .env (local dev only — in .gitignore)
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xyz.supabase.co
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGci...  # Safe for client
```

### ❌ NEVER Do This
```typescript
// NEVER — service role key in client code
const supabase = createClient(url, process.env.SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY);

// NEVER — hardcoded keys in source
const key = "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...";

// NEVER — commit .env file
git add .env  // ← BLOCKED by .gitignore
```

### Cloudflare Pages Environment Variables
- Store `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` in Cloudflare Pages → Settings → Environment variables
- NEVER store secrets that should be private (service role key) in Cloudflare env vars for client-side code
- If a server-side Astro endpoint needs service role → use Cloudflare Pages Functions with secret env var (NOT prefixed `PUBLIC_`)

