## Google OAuth via Supabase Auth

```typescript
// src/lib/auth.ts — Google login (client-side)
import { supabase } from './supabase';

export async function signInWithGoogle() {
  const { error } = await supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth({
    provider: 'google',
    options: {
      redirectTo: `${window.location.origin}/profile`,
    },
  });
  if (error) console.error('Auth error:', error.message);
}

export async function signOut() {
  await supabase.auth.signOut();
}

export async function getSession() {
  const { data: { session } } = await supabase.auth.getSession();
  return session;
}
```

> **No custom JWT.** No manual token refresh. Supabase handles all of this.
> Configure Google OAuth provider in Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → Providers.
> Add your domain to Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration → Redirect URLs.

