## Input Validation Rules
- Never trust client-supplied `user_id` — always use `auth.uid()` from RLS
- Validate all user inputs before inserting to Supabase (length, type, format)
- Sanitize text inputs displayed as HTML (prevent XSS)
- Game scores: validate on insert with RLS — users can only insert their own scores

```typescript
// ✅ Correct — user_id comes from auth, not request body
const { error } = await supabase
  .from('bookmarks')
  .insert({ url: validatedUrl, title: sanitizedTitle });
  // RLS uses auth.uid() — no need to pass user_id manually

// ❌ Wrong — trusting client-provided user_id
const { error } = await supabase
  .from('bookmarks')
  .insert({ url, user_id: requestBody.userId }); // ← Spoofable
```

